# Where the frontend looks for the API.
#
# Web (dev):  the local backend.
# Web (prod): set in the hosting dashboard at build time.
VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:5000/api

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Capacitor / mobile builds
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Inside the app, "localhost" is the phone itself, so the default above cannot
# work: a packaged build MUST be given a reachable, absolute HTTPS origin.
# Vite inlines this at build time, so set it before `pnpm mobile:build`:
#
#   VITE_API_URL=https://api.bharatassist.example/api pnpm mobile:build
#
# Two consequences worth stating plainly:
#
#   * HTTPS is required. Cleartext is disabled in capacitor.config.ts and
#     should stay that way; pointing the app at an http:// origin will fail
#     with a blocked request rather than silently downgrade.
#
#   * Anything inlined here ships inside the APK/IPA and can be read by
#     anyone who unzips it. This variable is a public endpoint, which is
#     fine. Never put an API key, secret or token in a VITE_* variable.
#
# To test against a backend on your own machine, use its LAN address over
# HTTPS (or a tunnel such as ngrok) rather than enabling cleartext:
#
#   VITE_API_URL=https://192.168.1.20:5000/api
#
# The backend must also allow the app's origin in CORS — add
# https://localhost (Android) and capacitor://localhost (iOS) to FRONTEND_URL
# / the CORS allowlist in apps/backend.
